    "learn.title": "Improve My Business",
    "learn.subtitle": "Short, practical lessons for growing your craft business.",
    "learn.watchLearn": "Watch & learn",
    "learn.readLearn": "Read & learn",
    "learn.lesson.pricing.title": "Getting a fair price for your craft",
    "learn.lesson.pricing.body": "Most artisans underprice their work by leaving out labour. Add up your material cost, then add your hours worked at a fair hourly rate. Many artisans charge ₹150 to ₹300 an hour depending on skill level. Add a small amount for overhead (electricity, workspace, packaging), then add a profit margin of 15 to 30%. Compare the final number to similar handmade pieces nearby. If you're far below that, you're likely underpricing.",
    "learn.lesson.vishwakarma.title": "PM Vishwakarma scheme",
    "learn.lesson.vishwakarma.body": "A government scheme for traditional artisans and craftspeople. It offers recognition (a Vishwakarma certificate and ID card), skill training with a stipend, a toolkit incentive up to ₹15,000, and collateral-free loans up to ₹3 lakh at concessional interest. Apply through your nearest Common Service Centre (CSC) with your Aadhaar card. There's no fee to apply.",
    "learn.lesson.whatsapp.title": "Selling on WhatsApp Business",
    "learn.lesson.whatsapp.body": "Switch to WhatsApp Business (free, separate app from regular WhatsApp) to get a catalogue, quick replies, and automated greetings. Add your products with photos and prices to the catalogue so customers can browse without asking one by one. Use broadcast lists, not groups, to message customers about new pieces. Broadcasts feel personal. Groups feel like spam.",
    "learn.lesson.descriptions.title": "Writing descriptions that sell",
    "learn.lesson.descriptions.body": "Lead with what makes the piece special: the technique, the region, how long it took. Then describe how it looks and feels. End with practical details: size, material, care instructions. Avoid generic words like \"beautiful\" or \"amazing.\" Say what's actually true. \"Hand-dyed with natural indigo\" tells a real story. \"Beautiful colours\" doesn't.",
    "learn.lesson.instagram.title": "Instagram basics for artisans",
    "learn.lesson.instagram.body": "Post consistently rather than often. Two or three times a week beats daily posts you can't sustain. Show your process, not just finished pieces. Customers trust what they can see being made. Use five to ten relevant hashtags, mixing broad ones like #handloom with specific ones like #kalamkaripainting. Reply to every comment. Instagram shows your posts to more people when you're active in replies.",
    "learn.lesson.protecting.title": "Protecting your craft",
    "learn.lesson.protecting.body": "A Geographical Indication (GI) tag protects region-specific crafts (like Pochampally Ikat or Kondapalli toys) from being copied and sold under the same name elsewhere. If your craft already has a GI tag, you can apply to use it through your local craft council or cooperative. It makes your product more trustworthy to buyers and often justifies a higher price.",
